## Vercel Speed Insights Installation - Complete

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the ZipDrop Next.js project.

### Changes Made

**Modified Files:**
1. `frontend/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component
   - Imported `SpeedInsights` from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
   - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the root layout's body section

2. `frontend/package.json` - Added dependency
   - Added `@vercel/speed-insights` package to dependencies

3. `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated lockfile
   - Automatically updated with the new package and its dependencies

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I implemented the recommended approach for Next.js 14.2.5 with App Router:

1. **Package Installation**: Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` using npm
2. **Component Integration**: Added the `SpeedInsights` component directly to the root layout at `app/layout.tsx`, which is the recommended method for Next.js v13.5+ with App Router
3. **Placement**: Component placed at the end of the `<body>` tag to avoid blocking page render

### Verification Steps Completed

✅ **Build Test**: Successfully built the project with `npm run build`
   - No TypeScript errors
   - No compilation errors
   - Static pages generated successfully

✅ **Linting**: Ran ESLint with `npm run lint`
   - No new linting errors introduced
   - One pre-existing warning unrelated to our changes

✅ **Tests**: Checked for test scripts
   - No test script configured in this project

### Next Steps for Production

To enable Speed Insights data collection in production:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Vercel project dashboard
3. Go to the "Speed Insights" section
4. Click the enable button to start collecting performance metrics

The SpeedInsights component will automatically start collecting and sending Core Web Vitals data once enabled in the Vercel dashboard.

### Technical Notes

- The implementation uses the Next.js-specific import path (`@vercel/speed-insights/next`) which provides optimized integration with Next.js App Router
- The component is lightweight and won't impact page load performance
- Data collection only works when deployed to Vercel (will not collect data in local development)
- The component automatically tracks Core Web Vitals metrics including LCP, FID, CLS, FCP, and TTFB
